and of the spouse of the respondent, a parent or dependent person;

(f)	the need to preserve and protect the institution of marriage and to give protection and assistance to the family as a natural and fundamental unit of society; and

(g)	any other matter that, in the circumstances of the case, the Court considers relevant.

